there is sql table name student with field id, name,mobileno., pancardno., course, field, fees . write sql query to detect duplicate student

//approach 1

SELECT mobileno, COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM student
GROUP BY mobileno
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;


//approach2

SELECT pancardno, COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM student
GROUP BY pancardno
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;


//approach3

SELECT name, mobileno, pancardno, course, field, fees,
       COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM student
GROUP BY name, mobileno, pancardno, course, field, fees
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;


Show every duplicate row
To display the complete details of all rows involved in a duplicate mobile number:

sql
SELECT s.*
FROM student s
JOIN (
    SELECT mobileno
    FROM student
    GROUP BY mobileno
    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
) d ON s.mobileno = d.mobileno
ORDER BY s.mobileno;
This joins the original table back to the duplicate mobile-number groups so you can inspect all matching records.

Identify extra copies, not the first record
sql
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT s.*,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY mobileno
               ORDER BY id
           ) AS rn
    FROM student s
) t
WHERE rn > 1;
